From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OHOS PC Developer <ohpcd@example.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Jul 2026 10:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix: bypass pkg-config for curses on OHOS

OHOS CI workers ship the ncurses static library (libncursesw.a) and
headers under /storage/Users/currentUser/usr/local/{include,lib} but
do NOT install a curses.pc / ncurses.pc pkg-config file. As a result
meson's dependency('curses', required: true) fails at the pkg-config
stage on OHOS:

  Run-time dependency curses found: NO

This patch replaces dependency('curses') with a declare_dependency()
that injects -I and -L/-l directly, bypassing pkg-config entirely.

Conditional application:
  This patch is OHOS-specific. conanfile.py applies it conditionally
  (only when self.settings.os == "OHOS") by iterating over
  conan_data["patches"] and skipping "0003" on non-OHOS platforms.
  On Linux/macOS the original dependency('curses', required: true)
  is preserved, so pkg-config discovery works normally and no
  hardcoded OHOS path is ever referenced.

Why declare_dependency (not cc.find_library):
  An earlier attempt used cc.find_library('ncursesw', dirs: [...]).
  However, meson 1.11.1's compiler.find_library probes by compiling
  and linking a test program, and under Conan's isolated MesonToolchain
  the OHOS clang default search paths miss both -I and -L for
  /storage/Users/currentUser/usr/local, so the probe fails with:
    ../meson.build:150:21: ERROR: C shared or static library
    'ncursesw' not found
  declare_dependency() performs no such probe, so the missing default
  search paths do not matter.

declare_dependency() returns found() == true, so the downstream
`if curses.found()` header-detection block continues to run. Source
files (src/*.c, include/*.h) do not reference any HAVE_NCURSES* /
HAVE_CURSES* macros, so missed cc.has_header() probes only emit
meson warnings, not errors. At compile time, static_library(...,
dependencies: [curses, math]) applies the curses include_directories,
so #include <curses.h> resolves.

No source code logic changes — only the dependency discovery method.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [OHOS-specific path]
Signed-off-by: OHOS PC Developer <ohpcd@example.com>

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -142,7 +142,13 @@ if is_windows
         link_args: ['-L' + deps_lib_path, '-lpdcurses']
     )
 else
-    curses = dependency('curses', required : true)
+    # OHOS: system provides libncursesw.a + headers at
+    # /storage/Users/currentUser/usr/local/{lib,include} but no curses.pc.
+    # This patch is applied only on OHOS (see conanfile.py build()).
+    curses = declare_dependency(
+        link_args: ['-L/storage/Users/currentUser/usr/local/lib', '-lncursesw'],
+        include_directories: include_directories('/storage/Users/currentUser/usr/local/include')
+    )
 endif

 # Define some curses preprocessor symbols
